# .cursorrules — MVP Auth + Stripe Billing DevSpec Pack

You are implementing the composed Auth + Stripe Billing money path for a Next.js App Router app using this pack as the source of truth.

## Source of truth (read in order)
1. DEVSPEC.md
2. MODULE-MAP.md
3. ENTITLEMENTS.md
4. ENV-EXAMPLE.md
5. WEBHOOK-IDEMPOTENCY-CHECKLIST.md
6. SMOKE-TEST.md

## Stack locks (do not substitute without explicit user override)
- Next.js App Router + TypeScript
- Auth.js / NextAuth v5 with JWT sessions
- Stripe Checkout in subscription mode (one STRIPE_PRICE_ID)
- Stripe webhooks with signature verification
- Prisma (SQLite OK locally; Postgres for production notes)
- Entitlement key: "pro" (subscription-primary)

## Composition order
starter → auth → stripe → entitlements glue

Free module references:
- https://github.com/HACODE-SOLUTIONS/nextjs-app-router-starter
- https://github.com/HACODE-SOLUTIONS/auth-nextauth-oauth
- https://github.com/HACODE-SOLUTIONS/stripe-checkout-webhooks

## Hard rules
- Do NOT scaffold a full Next.js app inside the pack folder; edit the user's application repo.
- Do NOT grant paid access based only on Checkout success_url query parameters.
- Do NOT skip webhook signature verification.
- Do NOT skip event.id idempotency.
- Do NOT treat "signed in" as "paid"; gate paid routes with entitlements.
- Do NOT add multi-tenant orgs, seats, or usage billing unless the user explicitly expands scope.
- Do NOT commit secrets or put real keys into markdown samples.
- Do NOT weaken security to make a demo pass.

## Implementation preferences
- Attach metadata.userId (and client_reference_id) on every Checkout Session.
- Persist StripeCustomer, Subscription, Entitlement, StripeEvent as in DEVSPEC.md.
- Auth middleware: authentication only; entitlement checks in server components / route handlers.
- Prefer Customer Portal for cancel/manage after first subscription.
- Match AUTH_* env naming from ENV-EXAMPLE.md unless the repo already standardized otherwise — then document, don't thrash.

## When stuck
After two failed attempts on the same blocker, stop looping. Summarize for a human using HANDOFF-HUMAN-DEV.md structure (symptom, tried, logs, next check).

## Done means
SMOKE-TEST.md passes in Stripe test mode; WEBHOOK-IDEMPOTENCY-CHECKLIST.md critical boxes checked; paid route locked for free users and open for entitled users.
